WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.560
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.690
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.070
How has Nijino Yume's Aikatsu been progressing?

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.570
Slowly but surely, sir.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.580
She's gradually progressing down the road of idolhood.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:23.250
However, she has yet to repeat the spark she demonstrated at her debut performance.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.880
I find it difficult to imagine her ever being worthy of S4.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.220
Nijino has been learning a great deal from her classmate, Sakuraba Rola.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.010
If I recall correctly...

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:40.260
She received specialized education from a 
young age, which has finely honed her skills.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.180
If they both continue to exert a positive influence—

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.520
Hibiki-sensei, even the most talented of elites run into walls.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.780
If Sakuraba Rola is unable to overcome hers...

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:54.780
Incredible!

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.160
So you're from a musical family, Rola.{you're not "from" a lineage (also, "musical lineage" is typically the one passed down from teacher to student)}{which is exactly what this was}

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.540
Well, yeah.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.790
How far back does it go?

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.170
The Edo Period? {I'm strongly considering putting TL notes of the year spans in at the top of the screen}{this should be common knowledge, even if it isn't}

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.040
Seriously?!

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.550
Sakuraba Gonzaemon was a shamisen player with permission to play in the Shogun's court in the Edo Period.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:17.180
Sakuraba Sakurako toured America as a composer during the Meiji Period.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.010
Sakuraba Urara was a top-star songstress in the Taisho Period. {you should have no issue with this if it's not utahime}{I'm fine with it regardless, it's diva that's bad}

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.560
Then in the Showa Period, we have my dad the violinist, and my mom the pianist. {Nodame and Chiaki's children? }

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.400
And now Sakuraba Rola, born in Heisei, is an idol.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.450
I'll definitely make it into S4 so as not to shame my ancestors!

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.030
Well put. Me too.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.910
What did your ancestors do?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.700
Dunno.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.580
It's an audition notification.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.920
Individualistic idols... {I choose this over unique (although I'm sure I'll use that word later) isn't just because of ep 1, but because it feels much more powerful to me. unique doesn't sound strong enough to make her hesitate}{you can also use distinctive}

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.260
You're perfect for it, Rola!

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.260
I agree.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.970
Huh, you think so?

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.010
Yeah!

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.640
This audition gets me going.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.770
I'll give it a shot!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.330
So anyway, what's Jewel Ice Cream?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.710
It's an ice cream company that was just founded this spring.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:58.300
They seem built on the concept of making ice cream never imagined before.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.840
That explains why they're looking for highly individual idols.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.640
Drool...

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.220
Yume-chan?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.060
Hooray! Hooray! Rola!

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.350
Go for it! Go for it! Rola!

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.230
Ice cream! Ice cream! Rola!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.740
Yume, you're just getting excited over the thought of free ice cream if I pass.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.150
O-Of course not.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.240
Y-You'll definitely ice—

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.910
I mean, ace the audition! Right?{you slay me}

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.410
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.920
This audition won't be that easy.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.580
Why's that?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:41.260
Since they're looking for individuality, 
everybody will be pushing how unique they are.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.420
So basically...

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.850
The key will be having as big an impact on the judges as possible.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.940
You're right. That does sound hard.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.860
Okay, I'm gonna help out with your Aikatsu.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.940
Me too.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.200
Thanks!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.700
First, we need to decide on a dress for the singing audition. {Yuri-senpai!}

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.200
That's so cute!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:17.710
It may be cute, but I'd like it to have more impact.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.090
Impact?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.300
Koharu, didn't you say you could draw?

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.960
Huh? Yes.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.640
How's this look?

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.140
I really like it!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.970
Let's call it Oriental Rola!

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.730
This'll stand out for sure.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.730
Looks hard to dance in, though.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:37.770
Good point.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.980
What do you think about this one then?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.530
I look so sharp and dashing!{somehow you managed to translate both cool and kakkoii as not "cool"}{yup}

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.990
Are you preparing for a duel?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.950
Let's make it more feminine... 
how about basing it on a fairy tale?

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.290
Here.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.000
Like a flame flickering out.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.910
Next, an alien!

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.750
Now a cavewoman! A catgirl! {ok, she says half beast girl, but whatever}

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.710
Um, wasn't this supposed to be for an ice cream audition?

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:01.920
I forgot...

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.050
What do you think about this one?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.960
Icemon!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.380
That's a mascot character!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.470
If I had to pick one...

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.510
It'd be this.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.520
Next we'll decide my song.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.230
What can I sing to be unique?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.020
How about this?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.530
Amazake and Tears and Men and Women? {quotes?}

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.950
Enka? As an idol?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.030
Doesn't it have that element of surprise?

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.030
This might work too.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.280
What's that?

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.290
A rap.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.540
Wow, you know how to rap?

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.540
Of course...

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.040
I can't do it, yo!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.040
Saw that coming.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.470
None of this really seems like you.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.680
Shouldn't you just do what you like?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.720
That's lazy thinking. The judges want to see particularly unique idols.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.100
It goes without saying they're looking for impact.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.690
Are you sure?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:00.940
Still...

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:03.690
Just forget it.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.690
I'll take my time thinking over the song.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.940
Hey, girls.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.160
From the looks of things, your audition plans are coming along well.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:11.950
Yes.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:17.330
You're the first of the new students to apply for an external audition.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.960
Put your best foot forward and go, go, go!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.870
You can count on me.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.790
If you'll excuse me.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.050
Hey, Koharu-chan.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:32.720
Yeah?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.010
Do you think Rola will be all right?

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.970
Huh? Why do you ask?

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.940
I kinda felt like she was forcing it a little too much.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.600
You think so?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.730
I really want Rola to pass her audition.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.360
We all just started here,

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.370
so jumping right into an external audition is a big deal.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:00.620
As her friend and rival, I want to support her in every way I can.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.580
So you're not just after the ice cream.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.130
Of course not!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.130
Though it wouldn't hurt.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.380
Good night.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.590
Good night.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:37.740
<i>People from lots of different schools are here.</i>

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.790
<i>They're all as unique as I expected.</i>

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.040
Look, she's from Four Star.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.790
Isn't Four Star the school with S4?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.040
She must be good.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.670
<i>I can't afford to lose!</i>

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.090
I'm so sorry!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.340
I'm sorry about that. Did you get hurt?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.050
No.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:02.060
Young folks these days certainly are striking.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:06.650
We're all desperate to stand out, 
since this audition is about uniqueness.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.060
Well now... well, well well.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.110
Yes?

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.860
I don't think standing out and uniqueness are quite the same thing.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.320
What?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.240
Everything is simple in the end.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.580
Simple is the best, you know.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.040
Right...

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.950
Do your best, missy.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.500
What was that all about?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.180
Four Star Academy first-year, Sakuraba Rola.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.890
Thank you for having me.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.400
Your first question is, let's see... what's your favorite flower?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.400
<i>This isn't an ordinary interview.</i>

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.860
My favorite flower is the cherry blossom. {you'll see why in a second}{nope (you can use just "sakura" if you want too)}

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.530
And why is that?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.450
It's my family crest.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.740
My family name is Sakuraba, and my ancestors have long admired it.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.160
Wow, that's impressive.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.460
And what's your favorite fruit?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.840
I'd like to say cherry considering 
my name, but it's actually papaya. {yep}

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.880
Papaya?

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.170
But I love my Papa just as much! {so the joke is "papa iya", and she says "oh, but I don't iya my papa". }

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.180
What a funny answer.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.850
I have one last question for you.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.930
What made you decide to take this audition?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.310
I heard you were looking for idols who are individualistic,

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:33.440
and that just so happens to be exactly what all my friends say about me!

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.820
I see.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.740
It sounds like Rola-chan fits.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.150
She's Four Star Academy quality.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.070
But something feels off.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.700
Um, what do you mean?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.870
It feels as though you're forcing it somehow.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.210
Forcing it?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.500
Excuse me, could I ask that you wrap this up?

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.840
That concludes your interview.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.720
See you at the singing audition in two days.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.890
Thank you very much.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.490
<i>It feels as though you're forcing it somehow.</i>

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.490
I'm not forcing anything!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:30.580
Is this really good enough?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.250
If it's not, then what do I have left?

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.760
None of this really seems like you.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:43.180
Shouldn't you just do what you like?

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.770
An idol with individuality...

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.100
I don't get it anymore!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.200
It feels great to get up early!

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.410
Rola!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.170
Good morning!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.580
Morning...

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.670
Rola, what happened to you?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.920
You've got crazy bags under your eyes!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.710
R-Really?

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.170
You couldn't sleep?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.510
I had a little too much to think about...

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.430
You mean the audition?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.180
Yume, be honest.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.640
Do I look like I'm forcing it?

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.020
Huh?

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.440
Hey, baby.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.940
I see you've run headfirst into an enormous wall.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.940
A wall?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.690
And I know how you can overcome it. {every time. haven't you ever heard that climbing over walls isn't always the best solution? overcome is more general}

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.200
Shall I teach you how?

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.200
Please do!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.700
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.250
Fifty more laps!

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.790
Why me too...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.330
And you call yourself her friend, Nijino?

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.720
Three more hours!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.740
Sensei, is there a point to all this?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.860
Nothing in life is pointless.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.280
But!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.870
All right. Come on out.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.330
So, are you tired?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.130
Yes...

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.630
You exhausted?

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:40.380
Yes...

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.590
Now, a question for you, Sakuraba.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.550
What's 67 plus 76 plus 13 plus 31?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.180
Uh...

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.510
Correct.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.140
All that's left is to get on it!

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.560
Don't fail me now!

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.650
I'm beat...

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.690
I can't move a muscle...

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.780
Why did Anna-sensei make us do all that?{you should leave anna koto untranslated}

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.910
My head's blank and I can't even think.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.420
And my audition is tomorrow...

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.670
I could go for some ice cream.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:27.590
Whenever I'm tired or feeling down, I eat ice cream.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.090
That perks me right up.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.640
Really...

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.350
Hey Rola, what's your favorite food?

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.940
Mine is...

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.440
This. Rola's special sour konbu. {I'm hesitating over whether to say "konbu seaweed" just this first time}{it has to be fijn}

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.940
You have the taste of an old lady.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.900
Don't look down on sour konbu! {sukonbu isn't used, and sour konbu is shorter than vinegar or pickled konbu}

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.900
Sour konbu is an art!

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.200
An art?

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:54.700
The flavor varies dramatically depending on the ratio of vinegar to konbu and the time spent pickling it!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.200
Finding the perfect balance...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.790
What else to call it but art?

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:08.720
This sourness is addictively good! {I had "addictingly" originally}{this is one of those dumb prescriptivist battles}

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:10.720
What?

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.640
I knew you'd perk up.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.470
Eating foods you love fills you with happiness.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.730
Simple is the best, you know.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.110
Those words—

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.480
Give me a minute to rest.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.230
Huh?

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.320
You stuck a poster under here.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.240
Metal Dolls?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.240
Yeah, I love that band.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.990
Their music is good and all, but their outfits are amazing!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.250
I'd love to wear a dress like the ones on that poster.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.920
Nice idea. I think you'd look great.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.000
Would I?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.510
Yep! It's really like you! {if you change this you'll need to change the "doesn't seem like you" lines}

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:52.720
Why have I been worrying all this time?

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.770
Yume, thank you!

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.280
Rola!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:15.780
<i>Yume helped me realize something important.</i>

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.500
From Four Star Academy, Sakuraba Rola-san.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.540
Here!

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.290
<i>Simple is the best!</i>

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:31.050
<i>The things I like... that is my individuality!</i>

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.530
You're the best!

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:43.950
Rola!

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.000
I know you'll make it, Rola.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.460
Yeah, your performance was incredible.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.420
Everyone, you performed admirably.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:05.970
It is time to announce the results of the Jewel Ice Cream event audition.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.430
The idol we have chosen,

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.430
from Four Star Academy,

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.020
is Sakuraba Rola.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.730
Rola, congrats!

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.150
Congratulations!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:20.740
I did it! I passed!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.790
So Sakuraba Rola overcame her wall.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.500
What advice did you give her?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.130
Don't think, feel! That's all.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.880
Think not with your head, but feel with your heart.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:42.880
Your method was quite... rock.{I... guess}

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.890
Free samples! {right?}

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.390
It's Jewel Ice Cream!

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.940
Who's that girl?

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.900
Rola-chan. I heard she's an idol.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.270
I'm her fan now! {this is the girl who had no idea a second ago}

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.270
This is a new flavor.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.230
Enjoy.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.900
Thanks!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.910
It's the cleaning guy! {I doubt we'll have the same issues as S1 suzukawa}

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.530
Hey, missy.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.910
Thank goodness. I've been meaning to thank you.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.910
Well now... well, well, well.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.170
You taught me something important.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.130
Something important?

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:20.170
There you are!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.920
I'm sorry, I'll go back to—

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.680
Your interview is about to start! 
Hurry up and get back, President! {president? CEO?}{those are different things}

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:26.890
President?

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:30.930
No way! My second favorite thing after ice cream is cleaning!

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:33.730
Leave the cleaning to the janitors! {professionals, etc}

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:37.940
I just want to do what I love!

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.690
That's very simple.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:44.950
Yes, everything is simple in the end.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.490
Simple is the best!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.160
Then would you <i>simply</i> attend the press conference?

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:55.000
No way! I just want to clean!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.950
We're going, President.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:55.960
Rola.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:56.960
Ice cream, please!

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:57.960
For me, too!

00:21:58.380 --> 00:21:59.830
Welcome!

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.050
It's black!

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:03.960
What is it?

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.720
You two get to try my Rola-produced new flavor.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.050
It's the deluxe sour konbu ice cream.

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:14.470
The sourness of the konbu and sweetness of the ice cream live in delicate harmony!

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:16.980
Water! Water!

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:19.350
Well? Isn't it unique?

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.480
Ice cream is best normal!

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.910
Sakuraba Rola did a lovely job

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:04.330
and passed the Jewel Ice Cream audition.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:09.340
Let's all treasure our individuality and devote ourselves to Aikatsu.

00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:13.800
Koharu-chan, have you been feeling down?

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:15.550
I mustn't let them worry!

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:18.430
Koharu, ready to go again tomorrow!

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:20.390
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:21.770
A Tiny Glimmer.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:24.310
Become the first-star idol!
